Jenkins — Freestyle Jobs: Complete Hands-On


For this lesson, build the following projects in order. This will take you from a basic Freestyle job to a small real-world CI workflow.


1. Create a Git Job

	Step 1 — Create the job

	Go to:

		Jenkins Dashboard → New Item → Freestyle project

	Name:

		git-checkout-demo

	Click OK.


Step 2 — Configure Git

Go to:

	Source Code Management → Git

Enter your repository URL:

	https://github.com/<username>/<repository>.git

Select the branch:

	*/main

If the repository is private, add your Jenkins Git credentials.



Step 3 — Add a Build Step

Go to:

	Build Steps → Add build step → Execute shell

	echo "===== Git Checkout Demo ====="

	echo "Job Name: $JOB_NAME"
	echo "Build Number: $BUILD_NUMBER"

	echo "Current directory:"
	pwd

	echo "Files from Git repository:"
	ls -la

Click Save → Build Now.



Step 4 — Check Console Output

Go to:

Build #1 → Console Output

Verify that Jenkins successfully checked out the repository.

------------------------------------------------------------------
===================================END==========================


