3. Create a Build Job

Create:

	application-build-demo

Add Execute shell:

	#!/bin/bash

	echo "===== Application Build ====="

	rm -rf build
	mkdir -p build

	echo "Building application..."

	echo "Application Name: DemoApp" > build/build-info.txt
	echo "Build Number: $BUILD_NUMBER" >> build/build-info.txt
	echo "Build Date: $(date)" >> build/build-info.txt

	cat build/build-info.txt

	echo "Build completed successfully."

	Run the build.

You should now have:

	workspace/
	└── build/
	    └── build-info.txt

.....................................................


4. Understand Build Steps

A Freestyle project can contain multiple build steps.

For example:

	Build Step 1

		echo "Installing dependencies..."

	Build Step 2
		echo "Running tests..."

	Build Step 3
		echo "Building application..."

	mkdir -p build
	echo "Build successful" > build/result.txt


The flow becomes:

	Checkout
	   ↓
	Install Dependencies
	   ↓
	Run Tests
	   ↓
	Build Application

If an important command returns a non-zero exit code, Jenkins can mark the build as failed.


For example:

exit 1

	will intentionally fail the build.
